# UX standards

**Full docs:** `docs/ux/` — start with [`UX_CONSTITUTION.md`](../../docs/ux/UX_CONSTITUTION.md).

## Non-negotiables (summary)

1. Use `--v-*` / Tailwind `v.*` tokens before raw hex or one-off sizes ([`DESIGN_TOKENS.md`](../../docs/ux/DESIGN_TOKENS.md)).
2. Use an approved layout pattern ([`LAYOUT_PATTERNS.md`](../../docs/ux/LAYOUT_PATTERNS.md)).
3. Reuse `shared/components` ([`ui-standards.mdc`](./ui-standards.mdc), [`COMPONENT_STANDARDS.md`](../../docs/ux/COMPONENT_STANDARDS.md)).
4. Light + dark mode for major module surfaces.
5. Interactive states: hover, focus, disabled, loading where applicable.
6. Empty states: icon, title, description, action when useful.
7. Destructive actions: confirm or Global Trash soft-delete.
8. Accessibility required ([`ACCESSIBILITY_STANDARDS.md`](../../docs/ux/ACCESSIBILITY_STANDARDS.md)).
9. UX changes must not bypass auth, permissions, or module boundaries.

## Shared Token Ownership

**No module-local design token systems** (e.g. `PlaceColorSystem.ts`, custom spacing scales). All colors, typography, spacing, radii, and shadows come from `web/src/styles/tokens.css`. Business branding may override tokens via the approved branding layer only.

## New UI

- Prefer `bg-v-surface`, `text-v-primary`, `var(--v-color-primary)` for new code.
- Legacy `bg-blue-600`, `--primary`, Tailwind grays remain until migration waves.

